ck-asm: attribution

This crate reads Fusion 360 (.f3d, .f3z) files. Its reader of the ASM B-rep blobs is MitCad's, adapted:

  MitCad, ASM reader (core/asm and core/vec3), version 0.70.0, upstream commit 806a4210126ab977ba678708dd476496ddbd2968
  Copyright (c) 2026 MitCad contributors, MIT licence (LICENSE-MIT-mitcad)

What came from MitCad, and what was changed:

  - src/asm/*.rs, src/brep.rs, src/convert.rs, src/history_states.rs, src/ids.rs, src/testdata.rs, ASM_FORMAT.md
    (core/asm, core/f3d/ASM_FORMAT.md): copied unchanged except for the points below. Every such file carries
    `SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`.
  - src/vec3/ (core/vec3): copied unchanged; it is a module of this crate here, not a crate of its own.
  - the paths `mitcad_vec3::` became `crate::vec3::` (src/brep.rs), the one unit test of src/convert.rs that checked the
    C++ builder's flat encoding (`flat.rs`) checks the flags the builder reads instead, and src/testdata.rs asserts
    `shell_is_closed_solid` where it asserted the flat encoding.
  - not taken: core/asm/src/flat.rs (the input of MitCad's OCCT builder), the rest of the MitCad tree.

Ours (this repository's own code): src/lib.rs, src/build.rs (the
neutral B-rep built into ck-topo), src/import.rs, src/container.rs, src/zip.rs, src/inflate.rs (the DEFLATE decoder of
ck-skp / ck-sldprt) and src/zstd.rs (a Zstandard decoder written from RFC 8878; MitCad uses the `ruzstd` crate, this
crate has no dependency outside the workspace). The format knowledge of the container entries follows MitCad's
core/f3d-file container reader.

Not used: the Autodesk Fusion or ASM SDK, or any file or code from Autodesk. MitCad's notes say its format knowledge
comes from inspecting files only. Fusion, ASM and Autodesk are trademarks of their owner and are used here only to name
the file format.
